    {"symbol": "📡", "tooltip": "Staged rollout telemetry is the runtime answer-key: the edge case nobody specified shows up as an error spike on 2% of traffic before it hits everyone."},
    {"symbol": "⏳", "tooltip": "A senior's mental model is also a decaying answer key — he misremembers in eighteen months or leaves in fourteen, so authorship was never the differentiator."}
  ],
  "claim_sketches": [
    {"claim": "A recovered-intent rationale is one whose claimed 'why' resolves to an artifact a machine can re-check: a test that demonstrably fails without the change and passes with it, a spec clause it satisfies, a code path you can step through.", "targets": ["AN-15"]},
    {"claim": "My view has always been that lab-bench testing cannot surface the harms that only appear in real-world use, so I won't pretend a fuzzer catches the refund path nobody specified.", "targets": ["AN-14"]},
    {"claim": "Human memory is also an externally-ungrounded narrative that drifts, and a stale human rationale is confidently wrong in exactly the way the Skeptic fears the AI one is.", "targets": ["AN-14"]},
    {"claim": "Mis-sorting is recoverable downstream, because boundary error is itself observable: a module classified 'standard' that starts spiking reviewer override rates and telemetry noise is announcing that it crossed the line.", "targets": ["AN-17"]},
    {"claim": "If mean-time-to-reconstruct on generated modules is worse than hand-authored after the pilot, I lose, and the trace step gets redesigned or scrapped.", "targets": ["AN-14", "AN-15"]}
  ]
