    {"symbol": "↩️", "tooltip": "You can roll back a generated module like an undo; you cannot undo hiring for a workflow that erased the people who held the design."},
    {"symbol": "🧾", "tooltip": "The defect that returns HTTP 200 never spikes a dashboard — the customer learns about it from their bank statement, not your telemetry."}
  ],
  "claim_sketches": [
    {"claim": "The pilot measures the reversible thing. You can scrap a generated module Monday morning. You cannot un-hire a team.", "targets": ["AN-10 + round-5 measurement plan"]},
    {"claim": "The failure class it structurally cannot see is the one that bills the customer. A refund computed wrong that still returns HTTP 200. A data field leaked with no exception thrown. No spike.", "targets": ["AN (round 5, runtime telemetry fallback)"]},
    {"claim": "A drifting senior is degraded provenance — you can walk to their desk. Generated intent no human ever held is absent provenance — there is nobody to ask. Degraded is recoverable. Absent is not.", "targets": ["AN (round 5, senior-PR symmetry move)"]},
    {"claim": "The binary grades correctness at a snapshot, not intent across evolving requirements; a valid-but-untestable rationale gets flagged as fabricated because no CI server re-executes a 'why we didn't do it that way.'", "targets": ["AN (round 5, test-binding mechanism)"]},
    {"claim": "Add silent-defect-escape rate and an irreversible-harm bucket, and name the kill criterion for the team-composition shift, not just the code — or the pilot proves the easy thing and is silent on the thing the debate is about.", "targets": ["AN-10 + round-5 measurement plan"]}
  ]
}

